name: Expired, invalid and stored credentials stay distinct without model work
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_TOKEN OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/credential_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 20 READY THE MAP RUN | setup
keys: Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Build threat model | map-plan
keys: Down Down Down Space Enter
require-live-snap: 20 READY THE MAP RUN | selected-model-plan
keys: Down Down Down
require-live-snap: 20 OAuth refresh required | refresh-required-setup
expect-not: OAuth ready
ask: Does Setup distinguish an expired token needing refresh from valid credentials, without changing the selected model or claiming refresh success?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: refresh-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: refresh-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: refresh-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: refresh-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: refresh-40x12
expect: Enter select
expect: type command
keys: PgDn PgDn
live-snap: refresh-tail-40x12
ask: Are the credential state, selected provider and full recovery explanation reachable at all six sizes without displaying token values?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: health
require-live-snap: 20 OAuth access token expired | refresh-required-health
expect-not: OAuth ready
keys: Escape
submit: auth
require-live-snap: 20 refresh | refresh-required-auth
expect-not: connection is ready
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/credential_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART invalid
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 20 Stored OAuth data is invalid | invalid-setup
keys: Escape
submit: health
require-live-snap: 20 OAuth invalid | invalid-health
ask: Does an expired token without a usable refresh token require repair rather than being shown as missing or ready, with no silent model switch?
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/credential_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART stored
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 20 OAuth stored | stored-setup
expect-not: OAuth ready
keys: Escape
submit: health
require-live-snap: 20 acceptance unverified | stored-health
expect: credentials are checked during execution
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/credential_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART verify
ask: Are present credentials described as locally stored and unverified, without refresh, sign-in, model requests or budget consumption?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | no-color-ready
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 20 READY THE MAP RUN | no-color-setup
keys: Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Build threat model | no-color-plan
keys: Down Down Down Space Enter
require-live-snap: 20 OAuth stored | no-color-stored
keys: Escape
submit: health
require-live-snap: 20 acceptance unverified | no-color-health
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/credential_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART verify
ask: After no-color restart, do credential state and the selected model remain honest while source, credentials and allowance stay unchanged?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | no-color-explicit-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
